<title>SINGAPORE: FELS wins rig construction contract.</title>
<headline>FELS wins rig construction contract.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Far East Levingston Shipbuilding Ltd (FELS) said on Monday it had won a rig-building contract from Santa Fe International Corp.</p>
<p>FELS would be responsible for the engineering and construction of the Universe-class jackup rig, with drilling equipment supplied by Santa Fe, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said work was likely to begin immediately and delivery was expected at FELS' yard in Singapore in the third quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>The new rig would be able to operate in depths of about 122 metres seasonally, 110 metres on a year-round basis and withstand a maximum wave height of 30 metres.</p>
<p>The company did not specify the cost of the contract.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
